# Release tarballs. `make rpm-package` regenerates one of these on every build
# (`git archive --output=$(PACKAGE_NAME)-$(VERSION).tar.gz HEAD`), so it is a
# build artifact that happens to live in the source root. Four of them had been
# committed over time; ignoring the pattern stops the next `git add -A` from
# quietly re-adding the one the last build left behind.
fileengine-http-bridge-*.tar.gz
